        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Countless bee groups emerge from the water and land on boat flowers floating on the surface. During May in Eastern Sea, ripples carry those flowers across bee sea; the flowers are vibrant, as large as small boats, and spread like scrolls in a sea of flowers.",
      "chapters": [
        907
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_eastern_sea"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Bee sea connects to flower sea. Large numbers of water bees live there. They can fly only for a short time and are better at swimming freely in the sea. The yearly May arrival of boat flowers is their only chance to collect nectar.",
      "chapters": [
        907
      ],
